{"name":"Tea Party","hex":"#ffd7d0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tea Party","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various independent, fiscally conservative political groups in the twenty-first-century United States."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Various independent, fiscally conservative political groups in the twenty-first-century United States, taken as a whole."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tea_Party"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tea Party (play)","blocks":[{"text":"Tea Party is a play written by Harold Pinter, which Pinter adapted from his own 1963 short story of the same title. As a screenplay, it was commissioned by the European Broadcasting Union, directed by Charles Jarrott. It was the second film to be transmitted on BBC Television in the programme The Largest Theatre in the World on 25 March 1965, after Heart to Heart. It was first produced on stage in October 1968 as part of a double bill with Pinter's play The Basement."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/58/TheTeaParty.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea_Party_(play)","wikidata":"Q7691079"},{"title":"Tea Party (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Tea Party\" is a song by Estonian singer Kerli. It is featured on the album Almost Alice, a multi-artist compilation album which features music inspired by the 2010 film Alice in Wonderland released on 2 March 2010."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7e/Kerli_Tea_Party_remixes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea_Party_(song)","wikidata":"Q782715"},{"title":"Tea party","blocks":[{"text":"A tea party is a social gathering event featuring the consumption of tea, sometimes including light refreshments. Social tea drinking rituals are observed in many cultures worldwide, both historically and in the present day. There is a long history of social consumption of tea in China, depicted in words and paintings, as well as in neighbouring countries such as Japan. The custom of tea party spread from China to Europe, where it became part of European culture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Song_Dynasty_Elegant_Party.JPG/330px-Song_Dynasty_Elegant_Party.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea_party","wikidata":"Q277222"},{"title":"Tea","blocks":[{"text":"Tea is an aromatic beverage prepared by infusion of hot or boiling fresh water with fresh or cured leaves of Camellia sinensis, an evergreen shrub native to East Asia that originated in the borderlands of southwestern China, northeast India and northern Myanmar. Tea has a stimulant effect in humans primarily due to its caffeine content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg/330px-Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea","wikidata":"Q6097"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/85/Kerli_Tea_Party_music_video.png/330px-Kerli_Tea_Party_music_video.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/85/Kerli_Tea_Party_music_video.png/330px-Kerli_Tea_Party_music_video.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kerli pours potion into the tea before it is served.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKerli_Tea_Party_music_video.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Mary_Cassatt_-_Afternoon_Tea_Party.jpg/330px-Mary_Cassatt_-_Afternoon_Tea_Party.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimed